<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paropamisadae</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Paropamisade</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paropamisadae was an ancient province in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a> region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, around the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a>. It was among the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapies</a> of Alexander's empire inherited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I</a>. Following his conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya">Chandragupta Maurya</a>, Seleucus ceded these eastern territories to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>, a defining moment in the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>'s borders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paropamisadae.jpg" alt="Paropamisadae" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shuja_Shah_Durrani_and_Men_in_his_decorated_palace_Wellcome_V0050531.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
